 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Collection of Qualcomm GStreamer plugins with open-source deps only
 This metapackage installs the Qualcomm GStreamer plugins that depend solely
 on open-source components, providing support for video processing, machine
 learning inference, metadata handling, messaging, and inter-process
 communication. It excludes plugins that require Qualcomm proprietary
 dependencies (such as the camsrc camera source), making it suitable for
 environments where only open-source dependencies are available.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-qimsdk-batch
Section: contrib/libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for batching multiple stream buffers
 Provides the qtibatch element for batching buffers from multiple input streams
 into a single output buffer. Useful for efficient processing of multiple video
 or data streams simultaneously, reducing overhead in multi-stream scenarios.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-qimsdk-camsrc
Section: contrib/libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 qcom-camera-server,
Description: GStreamer camera source plugin for Qualcomm platforms
 Provides the qticamsrc element (and the legacy qtiqmmfsrc alias), a live
 video/image source that captures from Qualcomm camera hardware through the
 QMMF camera server. The server (qcom-camera-server) must be reachable at
 runtime, but is only recommended rather than required: this lets the plugin
 run inside a container that talks to a cam-server instance running on the
 host platform, instead of forcing the daemon to be co-installed.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-qimsdk-metamux
Section: contrib/libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for multiplexing video/audio streams with metadata
 Provides the qtimetamux element for muxing video or audio streams with metadata
 streams. Enables synchronization of media content with associated metadata such
 as detection results, classifications, or custom annotations in ML pipelines.

Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-qimsdk-metatransform
Section: contrib/libs
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GStreamer plugin for metadata processing and transformation
 Provides the qtimetatransform element for processing, filtering, and converting
 metadata attached to buffers. Supports transformation of detection boxes,
 classification results, and other metadata formats between different coordinate
 systems and representations.

